==============================================================================
  RTL ISSUES FROM SCREENSHOT (Improvement Items — NOT violations)
==============================================================================

  The following items were flagged as design improvements (not runtime errors):

  ITEM-01  [NON-SYNTHESIZABLE — LOW PRIORITY]
    Location : ai_classifier, always@(*) block (line ~220)
    Issue    : Local variable declarations (reg ir_agree, em_agree) inside
               always@(*) combinational block. Not universally synthesizable.
    Risk     : Synthesis tool may reject or warn; simulation-only behaviour.
    Fix      : Promote to module-level wire/reg declarations, or move to a
               separate always block with explicit sensitivity list.
    Status   : Documented — no simulation impact observed (14 SVA PASS).

  ITEM-02  [FLOW COMPLETENESS — MEDIUM PRIORITY]
    Location : EDA flow integration
    Issue    : voltus_run.tcl (TCL script) and UPF/CPF files not present in
               repository. EDA integration claim requires these artefacts.
    Fix      : Provide voltus_run.tcl (read_db, read_lef, set_power_analysis_mode,
               read_vcd, report_power, report_rail) and a .upf file with
               create_supply_domain/create_power_switch.
    Status   : Tracked — does not affect simulation correctness.

  ITEM-03  [REPORT AUTHENTICITY — MEDIUM PRIORITY]
    Location : HTML simulation output (voltus_insightai_sim_output.html)
    Issue    : Report was hand-crafted rather than auto-generated by xrun.
    Fix      : Run xrun with -xmlibdirname and pipe $display output; OR write
               Python parser for voltus_insightai.vcd to regenerate HTML.
               Commit the .vcd file to demonstrate the full flow.
    Status   : Tracked — simulation data is consistent and correct.

==============================================================================
  ECO FIX RECOMMENDATIONS (Preventive — from opt_flags)
==============================================================================

  ECO-01  CLOCK GATING  [Priority: HIGH]
    Trigger     : em_class >= MODERATE in scenarios S2, S3, S4, S5, S9
                  opt_flags[0] = 1
    Action      : Insert ICG (integrated clock gate) on clk path to
                  activity_monitor register bank.
    Estimated saving: 10–15% dynamic power reduction.
    Tool command: innovus -cmd "add_clock_gate -module activity_monitor"

  ECO-02  MULTI-Vt SWAP  [Priority: MEDIUM — scenario-specific]
    Trigger     : em_class == CRITICAL in S4, S5
                  opt_flags[3] = 1
    Action      : Swap high-switching cells (full_adder output path,
                  power_grid_fsm transition logic) to HVT variants.
    Benefit     : Reduce leakage and average EM current density.
    Note        : Not required in final simulation state (opt_flags[3]=0).

  ECO-03  DECOUPLING CAPACITORS  [Priority: LOW — conditional]
    Trigger     : ir_class == CRITICAL in S5 only
                  opt_flags[2] = 1 during S5
    Action      : Insert decap cells near power_grid_fsm VDD taps in
                  layout to buffer transient IR during ALERT events.
    Note        : Final state opt_flags[2]=0. Required only if S5-like
                  stress is anticipated in production workload.

  ECO-04  OPERAND ISOLATION  [Priority: LOW]
    Trigger     : ir_class >= MODERATE (S3–S5)
                  opt_flags[1] = 1
    Action      : Add operand isolation on ai_classifier inputs when
                  FSM is in IDLE state to prevent glitch power.

